From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WS-B <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:49:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] 0981 redfin: /dev/btuart, the WCN3998 Bluetooth UART
 (btuart=1)

New bsd/dev/sweet_geniuart.c: QUPv3 wrapper 0 SE5 (0x894000,
msm-geni-serial-hs in the stock DT) as a character device for
phone/bt/btd, with its interrupt (GIC SPI 606 = INTID 638, level,
through 0911's sweet_spi_attach). FIFO mode after Linux
qcom_geni_serial.c: 8N1, RTS/CTS (RFR watermark depth - 2), RX
watermark + stale timeout into a 16 KiB ring, TX watermark refills;
clocks from gcc-lito.c (vote 0x52008 bits 6-9 + 15, RCG 0x17600 rows
or the DFS level), pins GPIO 38-41 function qup05 (EAST tile). The SE
must hold XBL-loaded UART firmware (GENI_FW_REVISION_RO protocol 2),
else open() fails with ENXIO. ioctls: baud, flow control (off = CTS
ignored + RTS held, for the WCN399x power pulses), drain, flush, read
timeout, stats (phone/bt/btuart.h). Exclusive open; interrupt masked
while closed. read() also drains the FIFO itself, so a missing
interrupt only costs latency.
Boot-args: btuart=1 makes the node (default: no node, SE5 untouched),
btuartos=16|32 overrides the UART oversampling (default from the QUP
version as Linux). poke "b 0" state, "b 1" HCI Read_Local_Version,
"b 2" QCA EDL version request (device closed, chip powered by btd).
No rails are voted here: btd does that through /dev/pmem.
